I could not execute live web search (both `three_pai_external_web_search` and `WebSearch` were permission-denied in this session). I'm grounding the prior-art assessment on published, retrievable sources from my own knowledge and the experiment's own Jensen-floor result, and I flag the no-live-search limitation explicitly.

```
ROLE: novelty_killer  VOTE: red

CLOSEST_PRIOR_WORK:
- {cite: "Schuster et al. 2022, Confident Adaptive Language Modeling (CALM)",
   url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.07061",
   why_close: "Per-token confidence-thresholded early exit. A *calibrated* confidence
   threshold ALREADY exits low-entropy/predictable tokens at shallow layers — i.e. the
   exact 'boilerplate saturates shallow' behavior this claim names. The per-class knob is
   a coarse re-parameterization of CALM's continuous per-token confidence signal."}
- {cite: "Elbayad et al. 2020, Depth-Adaptive Transformer",
   url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.10073",
   why_close: "Per-token adaptive depth; compute conditioned on token difficulty. Second
   independent source establishing content-conditioned depth is published prior art."}
- {cite: "Willard & Louf 2023, Efficient Guided Generation / Outlines (also jsonformer)",
   url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.09702",
   why_close: "NOT cited in packet. For grammar-forced tool-call scaffolding (JSON
   delimiters, schema keys), constrained decoding masks/forces the token — these tokens
   need ZERO adaptive-depth tuning. This directly undercuts the 'boilerplate is the win'
   premise: the cheapest structural tokens are already free under structured decoding."}
- {cite: "SkipDecode 2023 (arXiv:2307.02628); LayerSkip 2024 (arXiv:2404.16710)",
   url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.16710",
   why_close: "Token-/position-conditioned layer skipping; packet correctly flags both."}

NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: NAMING-only, not a mechanism delta. "Conditioning early-exit on token
class" is a discretized special case of "conditioning early-exit on per-token confidence,"
which CALM does continuously and optimally. Partitioning into {boilerplate, value} is a
strictly coarser policy than CALM's per-token threshold — it cannot add mechanism, only
remove resolution. The experiment's own L0 result proves this empirically: per-class beats
best-tuned global by <0.5pp (0/90 clear 5pp), the Jensen floor — the global confidence
threshold already captures the structural signal. Mechanism delta ≈ 0, by construction AND
by measurement.

FATAL_COLLISIONS:
- CALM-style calibrated global confidence threshold already early-exits low-entropy
  boilerplate; the class-conditioned threshold is empirically redundant (Part B NEGATIVE,
  +0.46pp). Collision verified in ≥2 independent published sources (CALM, Depth-Adaptive
  Transformer) AND reproduced in-experiment (Jensen-floor, matches EXP-0006).
- Constrained/structured decoding (Outlines/jsonformer) makes grammar-determined scaffolding
  tokens compute-free, weakening the "boilerplate fraction f is the lever" premise the whole
  Part-B novelty rests on. Owed and uncited.

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK:
- CALM (Schuster 2022), Depth-Adaptive Transformer (Elbayad 2020), SkipDecode (2023),
  LayerSkip (2024) — packet already flags these; good.
- MISSING and required: constrained/guided decoding for structured output
  (Outlines — Willard & Louf 2023; jsonformer). Must be cited before any agentic-scaffolding
  efficiency claim, because it already nullifies cost for the exact token class in question.
- Optional lineage: Graves 2016 (Adaptive Computation Time) for content-conditioned compute.

RATIONALE: The part actually under test (Part B: structure-aware per-class threshold vs a
TUNED global) is the only thing that could be novel, and it is dead two ways: (1) mechanism
is subsumed by CALM's confidence-thresholded early exit (arXiv:2207.07061) and Depth-Adaptive
Transformer (arXiv:1910.10073) — two independent sources — so the "class-conditioned" framing
is renaming, not a new mechanism; (2) the experiment's own pre-registered, honest L0 confirms
it: +0.46pp over best-tuned global, 0/90 configs clear the 5pp bar, Jensen floor, an exact
replay of the EXP-0006 grammar-region death. Part A (agentic>reasoning, ~4.6pp) is a real
*measurement* but is delivered by the global policy and is itself not a mechanism contribution
— it is "early exit, applied to agentic traces," which is an application of published methods.
Additionally, constrained decoding (Outlines, arXiv:2307.09702) erodes the premise that
boilerplate tokens are where savings live. Weak novelty: KILL. RED.
(Limitation: live prior-art search tools were permission-denied this session; citations are
from published-knowledge with retrievable arXiv URLs, cross-checked against the experiment's
own Jensen result — the ≥2-source collision bar is met via CALM + Depth-Adaptive Transformer.)
```
